runit is a small init and service supervisor, with real manuals (smarden.org/runit).
runit-init runs three stages: /etc/runit/1 (setup, then the same /etc/rc.d/boot/*.sh
scripts situation uses, so udev, fsck and the fstab mounts keep working), /etc/runit/2
(runsvdir supervises /etc/service) and /etc/runit/3 (shutdown). Service definitions live
in /etc/runit/sv/<name>/run and are enabled with a symlink in /etc/service. Ships the
net (dhcp) and getty-tty1 services, and poweroff/reboot/halt wrappers that use
runit-init under runit and fall back to situation's own commands under situation.
It does not replace /sbin/init: situation stays the default. To try runit, add a
limine entry that boots with init=/sbin/runit-init.
Day to day: sv status /etc/service/*, sv restart net, ln -s /etc/runit/sv/x /etc/service/x
